```rust
fn build_tap(tap: &Tap, base_bpm: f32, verts: &mut Vec<Vertex>, idxs: &mut Vec<u32>) {
    let cx = lane_to_x(tap.lane);
    let z = time_to_z(tap.time, base_bpm, DEFAULT_DROP_RATE);
    let scale = note_scale_at_z(z);
    // Base tap note is unit cube; scale determines world-space size
    let hw = scale * 0.5; // half-width
    let hd = scale * 0.1; // half-depth (notes are thin in z)
    push_quad(
        verts,
        idxs,
        [
            [cx - hw, NOTE_Y, z - hd],
            [cx + hw, NOTE_Y, z - hd],
            [cx + hw, NOTE_Y, z + hd],
            [cx - hw, NOTE_Y, z + hd],
        ],
        [0.40, 0.60, 1.00, 1.0],
    );
}
```

The scale at `z=0` is 1.5, giving a note width of 1.5 units. Lane width is 4.25, so the note covers 35% of the lane. At `z=-50`, scale=4.625 gives width=4.625 which is wider than the lane -- this compensates for perspective foreshortening so notes appear consistent size on screen. The depth is 10% of the width to keep notes thin.

